/*  Versions of one name — `src/Interpreter/DispatchExpansion.cs` and `DispatchConditions.cs`.

    ★ Top-level functions that share a name are versions of it, told apart by the TYPE of one or
    more arguments, by a `when` condition, or both. Before anything is gathered, each version
    becomes an ordinary function under a name of its own (`fold given sum 1`), and the name the
    writer called becomes a function built of `Judge` and `If` that picks between them — so what
    is checked afterwards is that program, and nothing downstream knows dispatch exists.

    ★ The conditions of one signature are proved never to hold together, by reading each into an
    `or` of `and`s of simple tests (equality against a literal, a type test, either negated) and
    finding a contradiction between every pair — which is what lets an ordinary `If` chain stand for
    dispatch that does not depend on order.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// The program with every group of versions replaced by its versions and their dispatcher.
    Bind node or failure to expand-dispatch, given (the node program):
        Define order as a series of text.
        Define groups as a map from text to node.
        For each statement in program's children, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "BindStatement" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)):
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                Define group as the entry for name in groups.
                If group is void:
                    Define fresh-group as cast listed.
                    In groups, the entry for name becomes fresh-group.
                    Insert name into order.
                    Cast fresh-group's add on (statement).
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    Cast group's add on (statement).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define replacements as a map from text to node.
        For each name in order, repeat:
            Define versions as (the entry for name in groups but void is cast listed)'s children.
            If the number of versions is greater than 1 or cast has-mark on (item 1 of versions, ":When"):
                Define built as cast build-dispatch on (name, versions) or pass the failure off.
                Define held as cast listed.
                For each statement in built, repeat:
                    Cast held's add on (statement).
                Done.
                In replacements, the entry for name becomes held.
            Done.
        Done.
        If the size of replacements is 0, return program.
        // Each group stands where its first version stood, and nowhere else.
        Define expanded as a new node { the kind program's kind, the word program's word, the children a series of node }.
        Define emitted as a map from text to fact.
        For each statement in program's children, repeat:
            Define replaced as cast unknown-type.
            If statement's kind is "BindStatement" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)):
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                Define found as the entry for name in replacements.
                If found is not void:
                    The replaced becomes found.
                    If (the entry for name in emitted) is void:
                        In emitted, the entry for name becomes true.
                        For each held in found's children, repeat:
                            Cast expanded's add on (held).
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            If cast is-none on (replaced), cast expanded's add on (statement).
        Done.
        Return expanded.
    Done.

    // ── Building one group ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind number to bind-row, given (the node version):
        Return cast numeric on (cast field-of on (version, 7)).
    Done.

    Bind text to parameter-name-at, given (the node version, the number place):
        Return cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (item place of (cast field-of on (version, 3))'s children, 2)).
    Done.

    /// The same types, each once, in the order first met.
    Bind series of node to distinct-types, given (the series of node shapes):
        Define kept as a series of node.
        Define seen as a map from text to fact.
        For each shape in shapes, repeat:
            Define key as cast type-key on (shape).
            If (the entry for key in seen) is void:
                In seen, the entry for key becomes true.
                Insert shape into kept.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return kept.
    Done.

    /// A signature is `(signature [types] [conditioned versions] fallback-or-_)`.
    Bind series of node to types-at, given (the series of node signatures, the number place):
        Define found as a series of node.
        For each signature in signatures, repeat:
            Insert item place of (cast field-of on (signature, 1))'s children into found.
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.

    Bind series of node or failure to build-dispatch, given (the text name, the series of node versions):
        Define first as item 1 of versions.
        Define first-count as the number of (cast field-of on (first, 3))'s children.
        Define first-row as cast bind-row on (first).
        Define place as 0.
        For each other in versions, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If place is greater than 1:
                Define other-row as cast bind-row on (other).
                Define other-count as the number of (cast field-of on (other, 3))'s children.
                If other-count is not first-count:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the versions of '{name}' take different numbers of arguments",
                        "The one on line {first-row} takes {first-count}, and this one takes {other-count}",
                        other-row, "declare a version of '{name}' with a different number of arguments",
                        "Every version of a name is reached by the same call, so they all take the same arguments. Rename this one if it does something else.")).
                Done.
                Define first-gives as cast field-of on (first, 2).
                Define other-gives as cast field-of on (other, 2).
                If cast type-key on (first-gives) is not cast type-key on (other-gives):
                    Define first-said as "nothing".
                    If cast is-nothing on (first-gives) is false, the first-said becomes cast type-words on (first-gives).
                    Define other-said as "nothing".
                    If cast is-nothing on (other-gives) is false, the other-said becomes cast type-words on (other-gives).
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the versions of '{name}' give back different types",
                        "The one on line {first-row} gives back {first-said}, and this one gives back {other-said}",
                        other-row, "declare a version of '{name}' with another return type",
                        "A caller has to know what it gets back without knowing which version ran, so every version gives back the same type.")).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.

        Define signatures as cast group-by-signature on (name, versions) or pass the failure off.

        // Which arguments are dispatched on — those whose type differs between signatures.
        Define varying as a series of number.
        Define arg-place as 0.
        While arg-place is less than first-count, repeat:
            Increment arg-place by 1.
            If the number of cast distinct-types on (cast types-at on (signatures, arg-place)) is greater than 1, insert arg-place into varying.
        Done.

        Define built as a series of node.
        If the number of varying is 0:
            Define only as item 1 of signatures.
            For each version in cast renamed-versions on (name, only), repeat:
                Insert version into built.
            Done.
            Insert cast dispatcher on (name, first, cast field-of on (first, 3),
                cast condition-chain on (name, only, first, a map from text to text)) into built.
            Return built.
        Done.

        Define cases-at as a series of node.
        For each varied in varying, repeat:
            Define cases as cast listed.
            For each one-case in cast distinct-types on (cast types-at on (signatures, varied)), repeat:
                Cast cases's add on (one-case).
            Done.
            Insert cases into cases-at.
        Done.
        Cast require-every-combination on (name, versions, signatures, varying, cases-at) or pass the failure off.

        For each signature in signatures, repeat:
            For each version in cast renamed-versions on (name, signature), repeat:
                Insert version into built.
            Done.
        Done.

        Define dispatcher-parameters as cast listed.
        Define index as 0.
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (first, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Increment index by 1.
            If cast holds-number on (varying, index):
                Define either-cases as cast listed.
                For each one-case in cast distinct-types on (cast types-at on (signatures, index)), repeat:
                    Cast either-cases's add on (one-case).
                Done.
                Define pair as cast listed.
                Cast pair's add on (cast made on ("UnionType", a series with (either-cases))).
                Cast pair's add on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)).
                Cast dispatcher-parameters's add on (pair).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Cast dispatcher-parameters's add on (parameter).
            Done.
        Done.
        Insert cast dispatcher on (name, first, dispatcher-parameters,
            cast judge-level on (name, first, varying, cases-at, 1, signatures, a map from text to text)) into built.
        Return built.
    Done.

    /// The versions grouped by their parameter types: in each, the conditioned ones and at most
    /// one fallback — then every signature's conditions checked.
    Bind series of node or failure to group-by-signature, given (the text name, the series of node versions):
        Define signatures as a series of node.
        For each version in versions, repeat:
            Define types as cast parameter-types-of on (version).
            Define key as cast type-key on (types).
            Define signature as cast unknown-type.
            For each candidate in signatures, repeat:
                If cast is-none on (signature) and cast type-key on (cast field-of on (candidate, 1)) is key, the signature becomes candidate.
            Done.
            If cast is-none on (signature):
                The signature becomes cast made on ("signature", a series with (types, cast listed, cast nothing)).
                Insert signature into signatures.
            Done.
            If cast has-mark on (version, ":When") is false:
                Define fallback as cast field-of on (signature, 3).
                If cast is-nothing on (fallback) is false:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is declared twice with the same argument types",
                        "It was already declared on line {cast bind-row on (fallback)}", cast bind-row on (version),
                        "declare '{name}' again with nothing to tell the two apart",
                        "Versions of a name are told apart by one argument's type or by a 'when' condition. These have neither, so no call could pick between them. Rename one of them.")).
                Done.
                The item 3 of signature's children becomes version.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Cast (cast field-of on (signature, 2))'s add on (version).
            Done.
        Done.
        For each signature in signatures, repeat:
            Cast check-conditions on (name, signature) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Return signatures.
    Done.

    /// The node a version's `when` carries.
    Bind node to when-of, given (the node version):
        Define place as 1.
        While place is less than the number of version's children, repeat:
            Define here as cast field-of on (version, place).
            If here's kind is "atom" and here's word is ":When", return cast field-of on (version, place + 1).
            Increment place by 1.
        Done.
        Return cast unknown-type.
    Done.

    /// Something runs when every condition is false, and no two conditions can hold together.
    Bind void or failure to check-conditions, given (the text name, the node signature):
        Define conditioned as (cast field-of on (signature, 2))'s children.
        If the number of conditioned is 0, return.
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (signature, 3)):
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("every version of '{name}' carries a condition",
                "A condition can be false, and something has to run when they all are",
                cast bind-row on (item 1 of conditioned), "leave '{name}' with nothing to run when no condition holds",
                "Add a version with no 'when' — it runs when none of the others apply.")).
        Done.
        Define clauses as a series of node.
        For each version in conditioned, repeat:
            Define clause as cast unknown-type.
            Try to:
                The clause becomes cast condition-dnf on (cast when-of on (version)).
            Done.
            In case of failure:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("this condition on '{name}' is outside what can be checked for overlap",
                    "Two versions may never both apply, and showing that needs a condition built from tests this checker can compare",
                    cast bind-row on (version), "tell versions of '{name}' apart by this condition",
                    "A 'when' is built from equality against a literal ('node's left is 0'), a type test ('node is a num-lit'), either of them negated, and 'and', 'or' and 'xor'. Ordering and arithmetic are not part of it.")).
            Done.
            Insert clause into clauses.
        Done.
        Define left-place as 0.
        While left-place is less than the number of clauses, repeat:
            Increment left-place by 1.
            Define right-place as left-place.
            While right-place is less than the number of clauses, repeat:
                Increment right-place by 1.
                If cast are-disjoint on (item left-place of clauses, item right-place of clauses) is false:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("two versions of '{name}' can both apply",
                        "The one on line {cast bind-row on (item left-place of conditioned)} and this one can hold at the same time, and the language does not decide which of two would win",
                        cast bind-row on (item right-place of conditioned), "declare versions of '{name}' whose conditions overlap",
                        "Make the conditions exclude each other — a version for the narrower case and a version for the rest — or fold the two bodies into one.")).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    // ── Conditions, as an `or` of `and`s of tests (`DispatchConditions`) ──

    /// What a test is about — `node`, `node's left` — or "" when it is about nothing nameable.
    Bind text to test-target, given (the node said):
        Define kind as said's kind.
        If kind is "VariableReference", return cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (said, 1)).
        If kind is "PossessiveAccess":
            Define inner as cast test-target on (cast field-of on (said, 1)).
            If inner is "", return "".
            Return "{inner}'s {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (said, 2))}".
        Done.
        If kind is "RecordNamedAccess":
            Define inner as cast test-target on (cast field-of on (said, 2)).
            If inner is "", return "".
            Return "{inner}'s {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (said, 1))}".
        Done.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// A literal as something two can be compared by — or "" when it is not a literal.
    Bind text to literal-identity, given (the node said):
        Define kind as said's kind.
        If kind is "NumberLiteral", return "number {cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 1))}".
        If kind is "StringLiteral", return "text {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (said, 1))}".
        If kind is "BooleanLiteral", return "fact {(cast field-of on (said, 1))'s word}".
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// One test: `(test target literal-or-"" type-or-_ negated)`.
    Bind node to one-test, given (the text target, the text literal, the node shape, the fact negated):
        Define test as cast made on ("test", a series with (cast quoted on (target), cast quoted on (literal), shape, cast flag on (negated))).
        Define conjunct as cast listed.
        Cast conjunct's add on (test).
        Define clause as cast listed.
        Cast clause's add on (conjunct).
        Return clause.
    Done.

    /// The condition as a list of conjuncts, each a list of tests — or a failure when it holds
    /// anything outside the fragment.
    Bind node or failure to condition-dnf, given (the node said):
        Define kind as said's kind.
        If kind is "IsTypeCheck":
            Define target as cast test-target on (cast field-of on (said, 1)).
            If target is "", return a failure "outside".
            Return cast one-test on (target, "", cast field-of on (said, 2), cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (said, 3))).
        Done.
        If kind is not "BinaryExpression", return a failure "outside".
        Define op as (cast field-of on (said, 2))'s word.
        If op is "Or":
            Define left as cast condition-dnf on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define right as cast condition-dnf on (cast field-of on (said, 3)) or pass the failure off.
            Define both as cast listed.
            For each conjunct in left's children, repeat:
                Cast both's add on (conjunct).
            Done.
            For each conjunct in right's children, repeat:
                Cast both's add on (conjunct).
            Done.
            Return both.
        Done.
        If op is "And":
            Define left as cast condition-dnf on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define right as cast condition-dnf on (cast field-of on (said, 3)) or pass the failure off.
            Define product as cast listed.
            For each left-conjunct in left's children, repeat:
                For each right-conjunct in right's children, repeat:
                    Define joined-conjunct as cast listed.
                    For each test in left-conjunct's children, repeat:
                        Cast joined-conjunct's add on (test).
                    Done.
                    For each test in right-conjunct's children, repeat:
                        Cast joined-conjunct's add on (test).
                    Done.
                    Cast product's add on (joined-conjunct).
                Done.
            Done.
            Return product.
        Done.
        If op is "Xor":
            Define first-side as cast field-of on (said, 1).
            Define second-side as cast field-of on (said, 3).
            Define line-atom as cast field-of on (said, 4).
            Define column-atom as cast field-of on (said, 5).
            Define one-way as cast made on ("BinaryExpression", a series with (first-side, cast atom on ("And"), cast negated-condition on (second-side), line-atom, column-atom)).
            Define other-way as cast made on ("BinaryExpression", a series with (cast negated-condition on (first-side), cast atom on ("And"), second-side, line-atom, column-atom)).
            Return cast condition-dnf on (cast made on ("BinaryExpression", a series with (one-way, cast atom on ("Or"), other-way, line-atom, column-atom))) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If op is "Equal" or op is "NotEqual":
            Define negated as op is "NotEqual".
            Define left-side as cast field-of on (said, 1).
            Define right-side as cast field-of on (said, 3).
            If cast literal-identity on (right-side) is not "" and cast test-target on (left-side) is not "":
                Return cast one-test on (cast test-target on (left-side), cast literal-identity on (right-side), cast nothing, negated).
            Done.
            If cast literal-identity on (left-side) is not "" and cast test-target on (right-side) is not "":
                Return cast one-test on (cast test-target on (right-side), cast literal-identity on (left-side), cast nothing, negated).
            Done.
        Done.
        Return a failure "outside".
    Done.

    /// `Negate`: what holds when this does not — anything but a test, `and` or `or` falls out of
    /// the fragment, which reading it then says.
    Bind node to negated-condition, given (the node said):
        Define kind as said's kind.
        If kind is "IsTypeCheck":
            Return cast made on ("IsTypeCheck", a series with (cast field-of on (said, 1), cast field-of on (said, 2),
                cast flag on (cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (said, 3)) is false), cast field-of on (said, 4), cast field-of on (said, 5))).
        Done.
        If kind is "BinaryExpression":
            Define op as (cast field-of on (said, 2))'s word.
            Define flipped as "".
            If op is "Equal", the flipped becomes "NotEqual".
            If op is "NotEqual", the flipped becomes "Equal".
            If flipped is not "":
                Return cast made on ("BinaryExpression", a series with (cast field-of on (said, 1), cast atom on (flipped),
                    cast field-of on (said, 3), cast field-of on (said, 4), cast field-of on (said, 5))).
            Done.
            Define joined-by as "".
            If op is "And", the joined-by becomes "Or".
            If op is "Or", the joined-by becomes "And".
            If joined-by is not "":
                Return cast made on ("BinaryExpression", a series with (cast negated-condition on (cast field-of on (said, 1)), cast atom on (joined-by),
                    cast negated-condition on (cast field-of on (said, 3)), cast field-of on (said, 4), cast field-of on (said, 5))).
            Done.
        Done.
        Return cast made on ("UnaryExpression", a series with (cast atom on ("Not"), said, cast numeral on (0), cast numeral on (0))).
    Done.

    /// Every conjunct of one against every conjunct of the other holds a contradiction.
    Bind fact to are-disjoint, given (the node left, the node right):
        For each left-conjunct in left's children, repeat:
            For each right-conjunct in right's children, repeat:
                If cast conjuncts-contradict on (left-conjunct, right-conjunct) is false, return false.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return true.
    Done.

    Bind fact to conjuncts-contradict, given (the node left, the node right):
        For each left-test in left's children, repeat:
            For each right-test in right's children, repeat:
                If cast tests-contradict on (left-test, right-test), return true.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// Two tests on the same thing that cannot both hold.
    Bind fact to tests-contradict, given (the node left, the node right):
        If (cast field-of on (left, 1))'s word is not (cast field-of on (right, 1))'s word, return false.
        Define left-literal as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (left, 2)).
        Define right-literal as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (right, 2)).
        If (left-literal is "") is not (right-literal is ""), return false.
        Define left-negated as cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (left, 4)).
        Define right-negated as cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (right, 4)).
        Define same as false.
        If left-literal is not "", the same becomes left-literal is right-literal.
        Otherwise, the same becomes cast type-key on (cast field-of on (left, 3)) is cast type-key on (cast field-of on (right, 3)).
        If same, return left-negated is not right-negated.
        Return left-negated is false and right-negated is false.
    Done.

    // ── Coverage, and the built statements ────────────────────────────────

    /// With more than one argument told apart, every combination of their cases needs a version.
    Bind void or failure to require-every-combination, given (the text name, the series of node versions,
            the series of node signatures, the series of number varying, the series of node cases-at):
        Define declared as a map from text to fact.
        For each signature in signatures, repeat:
            Define spelled-key as a series of text.
            For each varied in varying, repeat:
                Insert cast type-words on (item varied of (cast field-of on (signature, 1))'s children) into spelled-key.
            Done.
            In declared, the entry for cast joined-with on (spelled-key, " | ") becomes true.
        Done.
        Define indices as a series of number.
        For each cases in cases-at, repeat:
            Insert 1 into indices.
        Done.
        Define going as true.
        While going, repeat:
            Define combination as a series of node.
            Define slot as 0.
            For each cases in cases-at, repeat:
                Increment slot by 1.
                Insert item (item slot of indices) of cases's children into combination.
            Done.
            Define words as a series of text.
            For each one-case in combination, repeat:
                Insert cast type-words on (one-case) into words.
            Done.
            If (the entry for cast joined-with on (words, " | ") in declared) is void:
                Define parts as a series of text.
                Define at as 0.
                For each one-case in combination, repeat:
                    Increment at by 1.
                    Insert "argument {item at of varying} a {cast type-words on (one-case)}" into parts.
                Done.
                Define count as the number of varying.
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' has no version for {cast joined-with on (parts, ", ")}",
                    "{count} arguments tell its versions apart, so every combination of them has to have one",
                    cast bind-row on (item (the number of versions) of versions), "leave a call to '{name}' with nothing to run",
                    "Add that version, or tell the versions apart by one argument instead of {count}.")).
            Done.
            // The last arg-place turns fastest, like an odometer.
            Define turning as the number of indices.
            Define carried as true.
            While carried and turning is greater than 0, repeat:
                Define next as item turning of indices + 1.
                If next is greater than the number of (item turning of cases-at)'s children:
                    The item turning of indices becomes 1.
                    Decrement turning by 1.
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    The item turning of indices becomes next.
                    The carried becomes false.
                Done.
            Done.
            If carried, the going becomes false.
        Done.
    Done.

    Bind fact to holds-number, given (the series of number numbers, the number wanted):
        For each one-number in numbers, repeat:
            If one-number is wanted, return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    Bind text to joined-with, given (the series of text pieces, the text between):
        Define out as "".
        Define first as true.
        For each piece in pieces, repeat:
            If first is false, the out becomes out joined to between.
            The out becomes out joined to piece.
            The first becomes false.
        Done.
        Return out.
    Done.

    /// What one version is called once it stands alone: `fold given sum`, `fold given sum 1`.
    Bind text to version-name, given (the text name, the node signature, the number ordinal):
        Define words as a series of text.
        For each one-type in (cast field-of on (signature, 1))'s children, repeat:
            Insert cast type-words on (one-type) into words.
        Done.
        If ordinal is 0, return "{name} given {cast joined-with on (words, ", ")}".
        Return "{name} given {cast joined-with on (words, ", ")} {ordinal}".
    Done.

    /// A version under its own name, its `when` gone.
    Bind node to renamed-version, given (the node version, the text renamed):
        Define copy as cast made on ("BindStatement", a series of node).
        Define place as 0.
        Define skipping as false.
        For each part in version's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If skipping:
                The skipping becomes false.
            Done.
            Otherwise if part's kind is "atom" and part's word is ":When":
                The skipping becomes true.
            Done.
            Otherwise if place is 1:
                Cast copy's add on (cast quoted on (renamed)).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Cast copy's add on (part).
            Done.
        Done.
        Return copy.
    Done.

    Bind series of node to renamed-versions, given (the text name, the node signature):
        Define renamed as a series of node.
        Define ordinal as 0.
        For each version in (cast field-of on (signature, 2))'s children, repeat:
            Insert cast renamed-version on (version, cast version-name on (name, signature, ordinal)) into renamed.
            Increment ordinal by 1.
        Done.
        Define fallback as cast field-of on (signature, 3).
        If cast is-nothing on (fallback) is false:
            Insert cast renamed-version on (fallback, cast version-name on (name, signature, ordinal)) into renamed.
        Done.
        Return renamed.
    Done.

    /// The function the writer called, built over the versions.
    Bind node to dispatcher, given (the text name, the node shape, the node parameters, the node body):
        Return cast made on ("BindStatement", a series with (cast quoted on (name), cast field-of on (shape, 2), parameters, body,
            cast nothing, cast nothing, cast field-of on (shape, 7), cast field-of on (shape, 8))).
    Done.

    /// The call to one version, with each argument as the dispatcher holds it at this point.
    Bind node to call-to-version, given (the text name, the node signature, the number ordinal, the node version,
            the node shape, the map from text to text bound):
        Define line-atom as cast field-of on (version, 7).
        Define column-atom as cast field-of on (version, 8).
        Define handed-on as cast listed.
        Define place as 0.
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (shape, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define held as the entry for "{place}" in bound but void is cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)).
            Cast handed-on's add on (cast made on ("VariableReference", a series with (cast quoted on (held), line-atom, column-atom))).
        Done.
        Define callee as cast made on ("VariableReference", a series with (cast quoted on (cast version-name on (name, signature, ordinal)), line-atom, column-atom)).
        Define statements as cast listed.
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (shape, 2)):
            Cast statements's add on (cast made on ("CastStatement", a series with (callee, handed-on, line-atom, column-atom))).
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Define call as cast made on ("CastExpression", a series with (callee, handed-on, line-atom, column-atom)).
            Cast statements's add on (cast made on ("ReturnStatement", a series with (call, line-atom, column-atom))).
        Done.
        Return statements.
    Done.

    /// One signature's versions in turn: each condition, then the fallback.
    Bind node to condition-chain, given (the text name, the node signature, the node shape, the map from text to text bound):
        Define conditioned as (cast field-of on (signature, 2))'s children.
        Define fallback as cast field-of on (signature, 3).
        If the number of conditioned is 0:
            Return cast call-to-version on (name, signature, 0, fallback, shape, bound).
        Done.
        Define arms as cast listed.
        Define ordinal as 0.
        For each version in conditioned, repeat:
            // Inside a judgement the parameter still holds the whole union; the condition reads
            // the narrowed name instead.
            Define condition as cast when-of on (version).
            Define place as 0.
            For each parameter in (cast field-of on (shape, 3))'s children, repeat:
                Increment place by 1.
                Define parameter-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)).
                Define held as the entry for "{place}" in bound but void is "".
                If held is not "" and held is not parameter-name, the condition becomes cast renamed-in on (condition, parameter-name, held).
            Done.
            Cast arms's add on (cast made on ("ConditionArm", a series with (condition,
                cast call-to-version on (name, signature, ordinal, version, shape, bound)))).
            Increment ordinal by 1.
        Done.
        Define chain as cast listed.
        Cast chain's add on (cast made on ("IfStatement", a series with (arms, cast call-to-version on (name, signature, ordinal, fallback, shape, bound)))).
        Return chain.
    Done.

    /// The condition with one name swapped for another, through the shapes a `when` may hold.
    Bind node to renamed-in, given (the node said, the text old-name, the text new-name):
        Define kind as said's kind.
        If kind is "VariableReference":
            If cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) is not old-name, return said.
            Return cast made on ("VariableReference", a series with (cast quoted on (new-name), cast field-of on (said, 2), cast field-of on (said, 3))).
        Done.
        Define place as 0.
        If kind is "BinaryExpression" or kind is "UnaryExpression" or kind is "IsTypeCheck" or kind is "PossessiveAccess" or kind is "RecordNamedAccess":
            Define copy as cast made on (kind, a series of node).
            For each part in said's children, repeat:
                Increment place by 1.
                Define walked as false.
                If kind is "BinaryExpression" and (place is 1 or place is 3), the walked becomes true.
                If kind is "UnaryExpression" and place is 2, the walked becomes true.
                If (kind is "IsTypeCheck" or kind is "PossessiveAccess") and place is 1, the walked becomes true.
                If kind is "RecordNamedAccess" and place is 2, the walked becomes true.
                If walked, cast copy's add on (cast renamed-in on (part, old-name, new-name)).
                Otherwise, cast copy's add on (part).
            Done.
            Return copy.
        Done.
        Return said.
    Done.

    /// One `Judge` per argument told apart by type, nested, the innermost running that combination.
    Bind node to judge-level, given (the text name, the node shape, the series of number varying, the series of node cases-at,
            the number depth, the series of node remaining, the map from text to text bound):
        Define arg-place as item depth of varying.
        Define last as depth is the number of varying.
        Define line-atom as cast field-of on (shape, 7).
        Define column-atom as cast field-of on (shape, 8).
        Define arms as cast listed.
        Define case-place as 0.
        For each one-case in (item depth of cases-at)'s children, repeat:
            Increment case-place by 1.
            Define inner as a series of node.
            For each signature in remaining, repeat:
                If cast type-key on (item arg-place of (cast field-of on (signature, 1))'s children) is cast type-key on (one-case), insert signature into inner.
            Done.
            If the number of inner is greater than 0:
                Define body as cast listed.
                Define inner-bound as a map from text to text.
                For each mapping in bound, repeat:
                    In inner-bound, the entry for the key of mapping becomes the value of mapping.
                Done.
                If last:
                    In inner-bound, the entry for "{arg-place}" becomes "it".
                    For each statement in (cast condition-chain on (name, item 1 of inner, shape, inner-bound))'s children, repeat:
                        Cast body's add on (statement).
                    Done.
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    Define held as "{cast parameter-name-at on (shape, arg-place)} at {cast type-words on (one-case)} {depth - 1}.{case-place - 1}".
                    In inner-bound, the entry for "{arg-place}" becomes held.
                    Cast body's add on (cast made on ("DefineStatement", a series with (cast quoted on (held),
                        cast made on ("VariableReference", a series with (cast quoted on ("it"), line-atom, column-atom)),
                        cast flag on (false), cast flag on (false), line-atom, column-atom, cast nothing))).
                    For each statement in (cast judge-level on (name, shape, varying, cases-at, depth + 1, inner, inner-bound))'s children, repeat:
                        Cast body's add on (statement).
                    Done.
                Done.
                Define anchor as cast field-of on (item 1 of inner, 3).
                If cast is-nothing on (anchor), the anchor becomes item 1 of (cast field-of on (item 1 of inner, 2))'s children.
                Define arm-cases as cast listed.
                Cast arm-cases's add on (one-case).
                Cast arms's add on (cast made on ("JudgeArm", a series with (arm-cases, body, cast field-of on (anchor, 7), cast field-of on (anchor, 8), cast nothing))).
            Done.
        Done.
        Define subject as cast made on ("VariableReference", a series with (cast quoted on (cast parameter-name-at on (shape, arg-place)), line-atom, column-atom)).
        Define judged as cast listed.
        Cast judged's add on (cast made on ("JudgeStatement", a series with (subject, arms, cast nothing, line-atom, column-atom))).
        Return judged.
    Done.
Done.
